														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2027922">
									

<p>One light year away? And we're observing it with fine enough detail to get that much about its biology? Hell, we're able to observe a small nonreflective object at all? Given that this thing would take millennia to get to Earth, if it were even trying to, and is probably only observable using anomalous technology to begin with, I'm not sure why this as much as Euclid. For that matter, why it's even an SCP at all, rather than just a weird thing the Foundation assigns one guy to keep an eye on.</p>
<p>And how can we possibly tell changes in velocity of less than 100&#160;m/s? That's basically nothing. This thing is a hundred kilometers across. 100&#160;m/s is a change in velocity of one body length every three hours.</p>

