			<div class="content" id="post-content-2028065">
									

<p>So&#8230; it is a giant jellyfish made up of smaller jellyfish?</p>
<p>As far as things go, this article is kind of dull. Nothing actually happens with this organism. It's just floating off in space.</p>
<p>It's important to note that 1 light year is almost 10 trillion kilometers, and almost a quarter of the distance to our next closest star Alpha Centauri. With this distance, calling it Keter or even Euclid seems unnecessary. There needs to be something else to justify its classification or it needs to be lowered.</p>
<p>Gamma Ray Burst should not be capitalized. Don't capitalize the second article A in Addendum 2.</p>
<p>Say that the mass of matter was designated SCP-2027-1 instead of putting it in parentheses(which, should also not be capitalized).</p>

